-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 1, Preliminary (ss 1, 1A, 2, 2A).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Section 1A (the simplified outline) is explanatory
-- and carries no rule: it is `inert` in the coverage table of NOTES.md.

§ `Part 1: Preliminary`

§§ `Section 1: short title`

-- src:25 | 1 Short title
-- src:26 | This Act may be cited as the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 1 (src:25-26)
GIVETH A STRING
`the short title of this Act` MEANS "Acts Interpretation Act 1901"

§§ `The dates of this Act (data, from the legislation history in endnote 3)`

-- The text gives no date in square brackets under its title; the legislation history
-- (endnote 3) records the Act's own assent and commencement.
-- src:984 | Act
-- src:985 | Number and year
-- src:986 | Assent
-- src:987 | Commencement
-- src:988 | Application, saving and transitional provisions
-- src:989 | Acts Interpretation Act 1901
-- src:990 | 2, 1901
-- src:991 | 12 July 1901
-- src:992 | 12 July 1901
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901, endnote 3 (Legislation history), first row (src:984-992)
GIVETH A DATE
`the day this Act was assented to` MEANS Date 12 7 1901

@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901, endnote 3 (Legislation history), first row (src:984-992)
GIVETH A DATE
`the day this Act commenced` MEANS Date 12 7 1901

§§ `Section 2: application of this Act`

-- 2(1): this Act applies to all Acts, itself included. 2(2): the application of this
-- Act, or of a provision of it, to an Act or a provision of an Act is subject to a
-- contrary intention. Whether the other Act shows a contrary intention is a judgment
-- the text leaves to the reader of that Act, so it is an input and is never guessed.
-- src:52 | 2 Application of Act
-- src:53 | (1) This Act applies to all Acts (including this Act).
-- src:54 | Note: This Act also applies to legislative instruments, notifiable instruments and other instruments: see subsection 13(1) of the Legislation Act 2003 and subsection 46(1) of this Act.
-- src:55 | (2) However, the application of this Act or a provision of this Act to an Act or a provision of an Act is subject to a contrary intention.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2 (src:52-55)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears in the Act or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a provision of this Act applies to the Act or provision` `a contrary intention appears in the Act or provision` MEANS
    NOT `a contrary intention appears in the Act or provision`

§§ `Section 2A: binding the Crown`

-- src:56 | 2A Binding the Crown
-- src:57 | This Act binds the Crown in each of its capacities.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2A (src:56-57)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Act binds the Crown in each of its capacities` MEANS TRUE
